    <briefdescription>
<para>CubicSpline B-splines fitting method. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fits a discount function to a set of cubic B-splines <formula id="402">$ N_{i,3}(t) $</formula>, i.e., <formula id="403">\[ d(t) = \sum_{i=0}^{n} c_i * N_{i,3}(t) \]</formula> <verbatim>  See: McCulloch, J. 1971, &quot;Measuring the Term Structure of
  Interest Rates.&quot; Journal of Business, 44: 19-31
  McCulloch, J. 1975, &quot;The tax adjusted yield curve.&quot;
  Journal of Finance, XXX811-30
</verbatim></para><para><xrefsect id="caveats_1_caveats000140"><xreftitle>Warning</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>"The results are extremely sensitive to the number and location of the knot points, and there is no optimal way of selecting them.&quot; James, J. and
                 N. Webber, &quot;Interest Rate Modelling" John Wiley, 2000, pp. 440. </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
